Step 4: Create the Student Model
Right-click the Models folder.
Select:
Add → Class
Enter:
Student.cs
Add the following code:
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;
namespace StudentRegistration.Models
{
 public class Student
 {
 [Required]
 public string Name { get; set; }
 [Required]
 public string Email { get; set; }
 [Required]
 public string Password { get; set; }
 [Required]
 public string Gender { get; set; }
 [Required]
 public string Course { get; set; }
 public bool Agree { get; set; }
 }
}
The model contains information about the student.
Step 5: Create the Student Controller
Right-click the Controllers folder.
Select:
Add → Controller
Select:
MVC 5 Controller - Empty
Click Add.
Enter:
StudentController
Click Add.
Replace the controller code with:
using System.Web.Mvc;
using StudentRegistration.Models;
namespace StudentRegistration.Controllers
{
 public class StudentController : Controller
 {
 public ActionResult Register()
 {
 return View();
 }
 [HttpPost]
 public ActionResult Register(Student student)
 {
 if (ModelState.IsValid)
 {
 ViewBag.Message = "Student registered successfully!";
 }
 return View(student);
 }
 }
}
Here:
 Register() displays the registration form.
 The [HttpPost] method receives the submitted form data.
 ModelState.IsValid checks validation.
 ViewBag.Message displays the result.
